1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[squeaking]

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
"The mysterious unknown."

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called...

12
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
[theme song playing]

14
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
[Kurapika]
Take this to heart.

15
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
First,

16
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
a genuine Phantom Troupe tattoo

17
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
has the member's number inscribed
on the spider's back.

18
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Second,

19
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
they don't bother tallying
the people they've killed

20
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
because it's irrelevant to them.

21
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
And third,

22
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
don't ever mention the Phantom Troupe
to me again.

23
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
If you do...

24
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
I will kill you with my bare hands.

25
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
TRICK x TO x THE TRICK

26
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[narrator] Leorio, has volunteered
for the fourth round.

27
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
If he wins,
the group's victory is assured.

28
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
But will he be able to do it?

29
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Hm.

30
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Okay, it's time to end this.

31
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Drag him off and send in
your next contender.

32
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
[Leroute giggles]

33
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
That's not possible.

34
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Wait, what?

35
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
I said, I'm afraid we can't move him.

36
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
His match isn't over yet.

37
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
I don't get it,
how is the match not over?

38
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
What are you talking about?

39
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
He's still alive,
just unconscious.

40
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Oh, don't you remember?
This was a fight to the death.

41
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:32,000
One of them had to either die
or admit defeat.

42
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
He's still alive

43
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
and he hasn't surrendered.

44
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
[laughs]

45
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
[huffs]
Talk about splitting hairs.

46
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Maybe, but you've gotta admit
she's right.

47
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
-I'm with Killua.
-[Leorio grumbles]

48
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
That's how it is?

49
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
All right, Kurapika!

50
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Get over there and put that loser
out of his misery.

51
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
I refuse.

52
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
[Leorio] What... huh?

53
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
[yelling]
What do you mean, refuse?

54
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
The fight was already over.

55
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
It was clear to me
that by the time I punched him,

56
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
he had already lost the will to fight.

57
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
I will not continue fighting a loser.

58
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,000
[yelling] Seriously?
What are we supposed to do?

59
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
'Cause those guys are claiming
the match hasn't even ended yet.

60
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
-I will leave that to him
-[Leorio] Huh?

61
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
He can decide his own fate
just as soon as he revives.

62
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Come on!

63
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
We don't have that much time
and it's running out fast.

64
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
We can't afford to just sit around here
and wait.

65
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
My mind's made up, Leorio.

66
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Oh, give me a break.

67
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Hey, I can kill him

68
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
if you don't want to.

69
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Killua?

70
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Never killed anyone before, have you?

71
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Are you scared?

72
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Whether or not murder is frightening
has never entered my mind.

73
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Regardless, this is a one-on-one battle.

74
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,000
You can't interfere.

75
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Fine, I won't argue.

76
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Except, if you were a team-player

77
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
you wouldn't be acting so selfish.

78
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Hey! You said something useful
for once.

79
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Do that more often!

80
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Don't you know you're screwing up
our chances?

81
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
That's true,
but it doesn't change my position.

82
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
You stubborn little idiot.
[grumbles]

83
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
[yelling] All right,
time for majority rule.

84
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Press O to kill the bastard

85
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
or X to let him live.

86
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,000
-[Leorio] Ready, and...
-[Tonpa snickers]

87
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
[watch beeps]

88
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
[screaming] Why in the hell
isn't it working?

89
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
I bet it's because we're the ones
asking the question.

90
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
[Leorio]
Huh?

91
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:48,000
It looks like the timers only work
for questions the Examiners ask.

92
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
I should have known.
In that case...

93
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Okay! We'll do it the old-fashioned way.

94
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Raise your hand
if you think we should finish him!

95
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Me!

96
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Hm. Oh!

97
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Whose side are you on?

98
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
A minute ago you were trying to get him
to do it, just like I was.

99
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
We're in this together.
Where's your team spirit?

100
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
I just don't see the point.
Not like he's going to change his mind.

101
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Hey Gon, why don't you think
we should kill the guy?

102
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
I'm with Kurapika on this one.

103
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,000
He was just about to surrender
when he knocked him out.

104
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
We should wait for him to wake up.

105
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
But there's no telling
how long that'll take.

106
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,000
I ought to just do it.

107
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
It's better if you don't force the issue.

108
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
You can't expect everybody
to share the same opinion.

109
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Yeah, well nobody asked for yours, okay?

110
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,000
[Tonpa] Hey, come on.

111
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
If you wanted to put it to a vote,
you kind of did.

112
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
[Leorio] Huh?

113
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Fine! If you want to wait, then wait.
Just see if I care.

114
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Leorio, wait.

115
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
[Leorio, seething]
What is wrong with these people?

116
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
[Gon] He's sulking.

117
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
None of this matters
if we get stuck here.

118
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Am I the only one who gets it?

119
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Let's just leave him alone.

120
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
[Tonpa] Fools.

121
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,000
He's totally falling for it.

122
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,000
The trap of majority rule.

123
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,000
When five people
who barely know each other,

124
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
trying to decide on something,

125
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
you'd think voting would be the easiest
and most efficient way to do it.

126
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,000
People tend to think that voting
empowers the individual.

127
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:31,000
But the truth is, it can just as easily
turn the majority against the minority.

128
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
When someone keeps finding himself
in the minority,

129
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
his opinion is always rejected.

130
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:41,000
His anger, alienation, and frustration
make him resent antagonize the group.

131
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Eventually, it tears the team apart.

132
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
After all, it's everyone for himself
in the Hunter Exam.

133
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
The feeling you get when
you're forced to follow a path

134
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
that other people set
can be a real pain.

135
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,000
It's annoying and makes you feel foolish.

136
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:02,000
But now he's all caught up in
the whole majority rule scenario,

137
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:06,000
and he's starting to use it
even when he doesn't have to.

138
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
And then, he made the mistake of
discussing the options

139
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
before he called for the vote.

140
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
He even asked for a show of hands.

141
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Majority rule in its worst form.

142
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
When people are just pressing buttons
on their timers

143
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,000
they've got anonymity.

144
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
But when you raise your hand,

145
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
everybody knows exactly
what side you're on

146
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
and who's straying from the crowd.

147
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:31,000
And if you're in the minority,
there's no chance for a rebuttal.

148
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
When someone's opinions
are constantly rejected,

149
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
they feel like
their voice isn't being heard,

150
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
and the group breaks down.

151
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
And in our case it means
all five of us will fail the Exam.

152
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:47,000
It's just a matter of time.
[laughs]

153
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
[Sedokan] The atmosphere on the other side
is pretty grim.

154
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,000
[Leroute chuckles]

155
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
I've been waiting for you.

156
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Hisoka.

157
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:31,000
I'm not an Examiner this year.
I'm here for revenge.

158
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Ever since the last Exam,
all I've thought about is killing you.

159
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
And today I get payback.

160
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
[yelling]
For all the scars you gave me.

161
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
[laughs]

162
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Those scars are but a symbol of
your incompetence as an Examiner.

163
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Don't blame me for your inadequacies.

164
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Shut up.
[chuckles]

165
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Now prepare to die.

166
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Two-blade style, huh?

167
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
All-direction four blade style!

168
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[yelling]
Take this!

169
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[Togari cries out]

170
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
I'm not done!
[huffs]

171
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
[Togari laughs]
Up, down, left, right,

172
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
you've got nowhere to run.

173
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:41,000
You're going to be cut up from every angle
by my endless barrage of blades.

174
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
You can't dodge my attacks forever.

175
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,000
I’m going to have you writhing in pain
and I'll savor every second.

176
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
[Hisoka] Hm.

177
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
And then you'll die, Hisoka!

178
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
[yells]

179
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Dodging your attacks
would have been difficult, you're right.

180
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Stopping your blades, however...

181
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
[Togari] Impossible!

182
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,000
It took me more than six months
of training

183
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
to master catching those blades.

184
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,000
My, my.

185
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
That was easier than expected.

186
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Nice try but... it wasn't good enough.

187
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,000
[Togari breathes uneasily]

188
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
[screaming]
Damn it!

189
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:43,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

190
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:47,000
HISOKA

191
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
[voice over PA]
First to pass the Third Phase

192
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Hisoka, number 44.

193
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Time elapsed, six hours, 17 minutes.

194
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
What's up, Gon, is something wrong?

195
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:41,000
Yeah.

196
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Oh, I see.

197
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[Killua] Hey...

198
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
It's looking more and more
like he's already dead.

199
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,000
What do you mean?

200
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Well, he's been lying there for
a long time now

201
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
and he hasn't moved or anything.

202
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
[Leorio] Damn it.

203
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
It's impossible to tell
from this far away.

204
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:19,000
Hey you, we want to go over there
and check his body.

205
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
What was that?

206
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
He might be dead already
and we just want to see it for ourselves.

207
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
It's like I told you before,

208
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
he's only unconscious.

209
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Yeah? Well how many hours do you think
we've been here?

210
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
You think we're just going to take
your word for it?

211
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Care to make a wager, then?

212
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Wager?
A wager on what?

213
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
[Leroute] On whether he's dead or alive.

214
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
What are the stakes?
What are you proposing?

215
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[Leroute] Time.

216
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[Leorio] Time?

217
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
[Leroute] We will settle our match
through gambling,

218
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
betting time instead of chips.

219
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Look at the monitor on the wall.

220
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,000
We'll each have 50 hours
with which to wager.

221
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
And bets can only be placed
in ten hour increments.

222
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
We bet until one of our clocks
reaches zero.

223
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
Gambling with time, huh?

224
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
We'll take turns deciding
what to bet on.

225
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
If your credit reaches zero,

226
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:35,000
you will have 50 fewer hours
to escape the tower.

227
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
What if you hit zero first?

228
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Fifty years will be added
to our sentences.

229
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:43,000
[gasps]

230
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,000
If you accept these terms,

231
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
I'll confirm whether he's alive or dead.

232
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,000
[Lippo] Leroute...

233
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Sentenced to 112 years

234
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
for trafficking endangered wildlife
and breaking gambling laws.

235
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:03,000
This kind of match is right up her alley.

236
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
[Leorio]
Man, that woman is crazy.

237
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Betting with her own jail time like that?

238
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Consider your answer carefully.

239
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,000
If you lose,

240
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:19,000
we'll all have 50 fewer hours
to clear the tower.

241
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Yeah, well nobody's asking you.

242
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
In case you forgot,

243
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
you're the one who got us into
this stupid damn mess in the first place.

244
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Very well.
You won't hear another word from me.

245
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,000
[Leorio huffs]

246
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Come on, we shouldn't be fighting
each other.

247
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
[Tonpa chuckles]
Keep it up, boys. Keep it up.

248
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
All right,
I accept your damn challenge.

249
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Okay.

250
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
I chose our first bet
so you may set the ante.

251
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Decide how many hours we'll wager on
whether he's alive or dead.

252
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
I bet ten hours that he's alive!

253
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
[chuckles]
What the hell?

254
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,000
He was just whining about Majitani
being dead.

255
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,000
[Leroute laughs]

256
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
All right then, let's confirm.

257
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Playing it safe, aren't you?

258
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
I thought you weren't going to say
another word.

259
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
[Tonpa] Ten hours, huh?

260
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
[Leorio] It's the smart move.

261
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Even if I'm wrong and he is dead,

262
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
then Kurapika will have won his round.

263
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,000
It's progress, at least.

264
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
If I bet that he's dead
and he's just out cold,

265
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
it's adding insult to injury.

266
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:44,000
[heart beats]

267
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
See, he's only unconscious.

268
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,000
[Leorio] So it seems.

269
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
[clock dings]

270
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,000
[Gon] Yes!

271
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
Leorio's taken an early lead.

272
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
-This is bad.
-[Gon] Huh?

273
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Maybe he won't wake up
no matter how long we wait.

274
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,000
I don't understand.

275
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Don't you remember,
when she walked by the guy on the floor?

276
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,000
What of it?

277
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,000
Well, I was pretty sure he was
already dead by then.

278
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,000
But when I thought about it,

279
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
I realized he's more useful to his team
alive.

280
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
As long as he stays unconscious.

281
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
See, if he doesn't wake up
before the time runs out,

282
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,000
their sentences will be shortened
by 72 years.

283
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,000
So, if he doesn't wake up at all,
then that means we--

284
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,000
That's my point.

285
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,000
So, that's been their intention all along.

286
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
[Leroute] Okay, it's our turn.

287
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,000
What would you like to bet on next?

288
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Let me see...

289
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,000
I say we bet on whether or not
he's actually unconscious.

290
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Huh?

291
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:57,000
[Gon] Oh, I get it.

292
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Hm?

293
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
[Majitani]
Wait, What? This wasn't on the note.

294
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
What am I supposed to do now?

295
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,000
When I woke up there was
a note lying on the ground next to me.

296
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
It said,
“Keep pretending you’re out cold.

297
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Hide this note in your mouth.”

298
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
I knew what I was supposed to do.

299
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,000
All I had to do was stay down
until the clock ran out

300
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
and we’d get seventy-two years off
our sentences.

301
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
But, now what?

302
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Do I stay down and keep pretending?

303
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,000
[Leroute] All right.

304
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,000
I’ll bet twenty hours
that he really is out cold.

305
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,000
[Majitani] Okay, I got it!

306
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:47,000
That’s the play, then. I’ll just keep
acting like I’m unconscious.

307
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,000
[Leroute] The question is, how do you
propose we go about confirming this?

308
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
[Leorio] Oh...

309
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,000
It's simple, really.

310
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Heavy bastard.

311
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,000
[Leorio grunts]

312
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
I figured I would just push him
off the edge.

313
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,000
[Majitani]
That’s the worst idea I’ve ever heard!

314
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
If he's really unconscious,

315
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,000
he’ll fall to his death
and that’s the end of it.

316
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Are you insane?

317
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
His match hasn’t been decided yet.

318
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
There’s no way I can accept those terms!

319
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Don't worry.

320
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
If he falls and kicks the bucket,

321
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,000
we’ll forfeit the match

322
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:37,000
giving you a grand total of two wins.

323
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
That work for you?

324
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
It does. Very well, then.

325
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,000
What was that?
Come on, don’t be ridiculous!

326
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
We’re talking about my life here!

327
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,000
[Leroute]
In that case, I’m changing my bet

328
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
I bet 40 hours
that he isn’t unconscious after all.

329
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
That’s everything I have left.

330
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:07,000
[chuckles] Little sneak.
Finally showing your true colors.

331
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
[heart beats]

332
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,000
[rhythm of heart increases steadily]

333
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Guess I'll let go, then.

334
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
[yelling] Whoa, whoa, whoa, hold on,
don't let go. I'm awake!

335
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
I'm awake.

336
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,000
[screams]
Wait! Wait!

337
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
I'm going to fall!

338
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Good morning.
[chuckles]

339
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
[Majitani groans]

340
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
You’re both complete lunatics!

341
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
I’ve had enough!

342
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
I lost plain and simple, okay?

343
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Forget reducing my sentence.

344
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
I’m going back to prison where it’s safe!

345
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Dammit!

346
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
[Leroute]
You knew he was awake, didn't you?

347
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Believe it or not, but I’m pre-med.

348
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:11,000
The way his eyes were moving
was a dead giveaway.

349
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
[clock beeps]

350
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Even so,
you have only twenty hours remaining.

351
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:23,000
I know. But at least now we’re in
a better position with a two-one lead.

352
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
[beeping]

353
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Now, let's keep this ball rolling.

354
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
The choice is yours,
so what’s it gonna be?

355
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
[narrator]
Majitani throws in the towel,

356
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,000
giving Gon and his friends
a two-to-one lead.

357
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:48,000
However, in the match
where they gamble for time,

358
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:50,000
they’re down 80 to 20.

359
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
It’s Leroute’s turn to pick the next bet.

360
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,000
But what will she choose?

361
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
[theme song playing]

362
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[Gon] Next time.
"Trouble with the Gamble."

363
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Bull... bull... bulldog!

364
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,000
[Gon barks]
